   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Cancer in the patient or family: could it be HEREDITARY, and WHO do I test?",
   "lines": [
    "most cancer is SPORADIC (one somatic cell, NOT passed on) or FAMILIAL (shared genes + environment)",
    "take ≥ 3 generations on BOTH sides: cancer types, age at diagnosis, new primary or metastasis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_her",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 774,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "A RED FLAG → suspect HEREDITARY (a mutation in EVERY cell, inherited)",
   "lines": [
    "early onset (breast < 50, ovarian < 60) · several primaries in one person · several relatives on ONE side · a family pattern · Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry (BRCA1/2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "p_ref",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 256,
   "w": 774,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "info",
   "title": "REFER for genetic counselling if ALL of these",
   "lines": [
    "• personal or family history of cancer",
    "• a test exists and its result can be interpreted",
    "• the result could change management, AND the patient wants to know"
   ]
  },
